Independent boot-test suite for golden guest images (kind `image-first-boot`).

  image-first-boot <image.qcow2>     exit 0 = all checks passed, 1 = a check failed, other = infrastructure error (no attestation)
  staticchecks.py                    offline hardening checks over an extracted image tree
  icssim.py                          throw-away ICS callback simulator (protocol pinned to ics.guest.callback by ics/tests/test_golden_prod.py)
  tcprelay.py                        qemu guestfwd helper (the guest can reach exactly the simulator)

Attestor contract (blueprints/build/repo/ou-test-attest `run image-first-boot <path>`, branch fixes-r7, attestation v2):
  the attestor copies the image into its private work dir, then executes <lib>/image-first-boot <copy> with env OU_TEST_KIND=image-first-boot, OU_TEST_WORK=<dir>.
  <lib> (default /usr/local/lib/ou-testrunner) must be root-owned, not group/world writable: install ALL files of this directory there with
  `install -m 0755 image-first-boot` / `install -m 0644 *.py` (see install-testsuite.sh). The program is therefore never taken from the builder's output.
Needs on the runner: qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-img, openssl, e2fsprogs (debugfs), util-linux (sfdisk), python3 + cryptography, ~6 GiB free in OU_TEST_WORK, 1.2 GiB RAM.
Run it inside a throw-away container with no network (the guest is untrusted code under TCG; the user-mode network is `restrict=on`).
